//! The `scroll-initial-target` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! enables the definition of elements that are potential snap targets when their ancestor `scroll
//! container` is first rendered.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - nearest: The element is potentially an initial scroll target for its nearest scroll container
//! ancestor.
//! - none: The element is not an initial scroll target.
//!
//! Grammar: none | nearest
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-scroll-snap-2/#propdef-scroll-initial-target
